PS5 HDMI: ps5-linux-patches #49, #50 and #54, ported from 7.2 to 7.3

#49 HDR output on FLAVA3: HDR10 as 12 bpc YCbCr 4:2:2 (same TMDS clock as
    8 bpc RGB) at 1080p60/2160p60, DRM InfoFrame and BT.2020 colorimetry
    through the bridge; sceHdmiSetVideoConfig() gets bpc and encoding.
#50 clear SCDC scrambling when leaving 2160p60.
#54 back off HDMI hotplug retries while DP link training keeps failing.
plus [ps5-bazzite-deck]: RGB output stays at 8 bpc on the PS5 (the bridges
show deeper RGB as posterized contours); the only deep-colour output is the
HDR 4:2:2 above, which (unlike upstream) doesn't depend on the requested
colour depth, since "max bpc" is 8 on the PS5. Drop when meower carries these.
---

